Q: Mikro Orm with nestjs does not load entities automatically A: <p>I've had the same struggle, the fix was in the <code>AppModule</code></p>
<p>For your example</p>
<pre class="lang-ts prettyprint-override"><code>MikroOrmModule.forRoot({
      type: 'postgresql',
      host: 'localhost',
      user: 'test',
      password: 'test',
      dbName: 'test',
      port: 5440,
      autoLoadEntities: true, // Make sure this is true

      // entities: ['../entity/domain'],
      // entitiesTs: ['../entity/domain'],

      entities: [User], // Just write out the entities you have, no need for path
      allowGlobalContext: true,
      schemaGenerator: {
        createForeignKeyConstraints: false,
      },
    }),
</code></pre>

Q: How to Load an .aspx page in Div with jQuery in asp.net? A: <p>It should be as simple as this, unless I'm misunderstanding something. Where is your JS / JQuery? I'm assuming it's on the main page where the menu is?</p>
<p>Also, is this on the same domain as http://mywebsite?</p>
<p>FYI, using .ajax instead of the .post shorthand gives you much more control over the headers.</p>
<pre><code>$(document).ready(function () {


    function loadPage(formData) {
        $.ajax({
            type: &quot;POST&quot;,
            url: &quot;http://mywebsite/ExternalPage.aspx&quot;,
            data: formData, // { id: 1, name: 'Jim' }
            crossDomain: false, // ?? 
            dataType: &quot;json&quot;,
            async: true
            //old way....
            // ,
            // success: function (result) {
            //     $(&quot;#divExternalPage&quot;).html(result);
            // },
            // error: function (e, Msg) {
            //     console.log(`Error: ${e} : ${Msg}`);
            // }
        })
        .done(function(response) {
            console.log('Success!', response);
            $(&quot;#divExternalPage&quot;).html(response);
        })
        .fail(function(jqXHR, textStatus, error) {
            console.error('Request failed:', textStatus, error);
        });
    }

});
</code></pre>
<p>Post your code on jsfiddle or something if you can.</p>
<p>Also, I didn't test this. Not 100% certain the fail function is correct, but you get the idea.</p>

