Q: how to integrate an android .aar library file into a flutter project A: <p>First create a libs folder in android root folder then adding your <code>.aar</code> file to <code>libs</code>(in your case <code>liblibrary</code>) folder in android root folder, add this in android <code>build.gradle</code>:</p>
<pre><code>allprojects {
    repositories {
        google()
        jcenter()
        flatDir {
            dirs '../libs' // in your case liblibrary
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>then in app <code>build.gradle</code> add this:</p>
<pre><code>dependencies {
    ...
    implementation(name:'your_file_name', ext:'aar')
}
</code></pre>
<p>then sync your gradle and you are good to go.</p>
